.venv/
_bench_tmp/
__pycache__/

# Derived artifacts. `build_corpus.py` emits pages/; `capture.py` emits shots/ and
# snapshots/. The generators plus manifest.json are the source of truth, and
# regenerating is two commands -- committing ~47k lines of rendered output would
# bury the evidence that actually matters (findings_dom.json, local_vlm_results.json,
# blind_key.json) in noise that changes on every Chromium bump.
corpus/out/pages/
corpus/out/shots/
corpus/out/snapshots/
corpus/out/blind/

# The router's queue is derived from whichever profile last ran, so a committed
# copy would be a record of one invocation wearing the authority of a baseline --
# and its crop byte sizes churn with every Pillow bump. `route.py` rebuilds both
# in under a second. The FP-gate receipt and the per-rule censuses DO stay
# tracked: they are the denominator every safety claim in the README needs, they
# are small, and they change only when a rule changes.
corpus/out/queue/
corpus/out/route_plan.json
